{title: The Hill Country of Seir}
{subtitle: Genesis 36:1–43}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 88}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] |
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] | [Eb] | ×2

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]This is the family history of E[Eb]sau, that is, E[Bb]dom
He took his wives from the daughters of Ca[F]naan
A[Eb]dah daughter of Elon, and [Bb]O[Bbmaj7/A]holiba[Gm]mah
And [Eb]Basemath daughter of Ish[Bb]mael
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Adah bore Eliphaz to Esau in the [Eb]land
And [Bb]Basemath bore Reuel, [F]sons born in Canaan
Oholi[Eb]bamah bore Jeush, [Bb]Jalam, and Ko[Gm]rah
Their pos[Eb]sessions were too great for them [F]to live togeth[Bb]er
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
The [Gm]land where they were sta[F]ying could [Eb]not support [Bb]them
[Gm]Because of [F]their livestock, [Eb]they had to move away
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
So E[Bb]sau settled in the hill country of [Eb]Seir
He moved [Bb]to another land, away from his brother Ja[F]cob
This is the [Bb]family history of Esau, the fa[Eb]ther of the Edo[Bb]mites
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Eliphaz son of A[Eb]dah, Reuel son of Ba[Bb]semath
Chiefs descended from them [F]in the land of Edom
[Eb]Teman, Omar, Zepho, [Bb]Kenaz, and Ama[Gm]lek
[Eb]These were the chiefs among [F]Esau's descen[Bb]dants
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
So Esau settled in the hill country of [Eb]Seir
He moved [Bb]to another land, away from his brother Ja[F]cob
This is the [Bb]family history of Esau, the fa[Eb]ther of the Edo[Bb]mites
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]Lotan, Shobal, Zibeon, [Bb]Anah, Dis[F]hon
[Eb]Ezer, and Dishan, the Horite [Bb]chiefs in the [F]land
[Eb]Seir the Horite lived there be[F]fore the kings came
{end_of_bridge}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Eb]These were the chiefs of Edom, ac[F]cording to their settlements
[Eb]This was Esau, the father of the Edo[Bb]mites
{end_of_verse}
